Just making a list of the items my human rogue needs to find.

I need a beartrap so I can get a unicorn horn so I can identify potions 
and gain poison resistance.

Either item at the end of Sokoban will help me take on the mines, but if 
I don't get the amulet then I'll need a silver shield to deal with all 
of those wand zapping gnasty gnomes.

A pickaxe is handy on the level before Sokoban to get some spellbooks. 
By their price ranges I can determine which are level one and read 
those.  Hopefully this will give me either light or detect monsters. 
(For the skill practice.)

Equipped with a light source and something reflective I can at least 
make it down to minetown.  If the priest is friendly I can invite the 
captain in and lock the door for an offhand silver saber.

After clearing out the mines if I have a magic lamp then it's time to 
get Magicbane, even if I need to offer a wererat for a conversion to 
upgrade the Gnome king's hooch.

Equipped with stone and 'bane it's time to camp for a bit then with the 
book of Identify I can go search for the things needed to deal with the 
"impossible" rogue quest.

Life is so much easier for Wizards who will have their third magic 
resistance item by the time they complete their much easier quest.

